From: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: enable ATHUB power gating on Navi 14

Navi 14 is the only navi1x that does not get AMD_PG_SUPPORT_ATHUB in
nv_common_early_init(); Navi 10 and Navi 12 both set it. The flag gates
FEATURE_ATHUB_PG_BIT in navi10_init_allowed_features(), so PMFW never
power-gates ATHUB on Navi 14. The feature bit exists in the Navi 14
PMFW interface (smu11_driver_if_navi10.h is shared by all navi1x).

Add AMD_PG_SUPPORT_ATHUB to the Navi 14 pg_flags.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nv.c
index 7ce1a1b95..2835e29bb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/nv.c
@@ -693,7 +693,8 @@ static int nv_common_early_init(struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip_block)
 			AMD_CG_SUPPORT_BIF_LS;
 		adev->pg_flags = AMD_PG_SUPPORT_VCN |
 			AMD_PG_SUPPORT_JPEG |
-			AMD_PG_SUPPORT_VCN_DPG;
+			AMD_PG_SUPPORT_VCN_DPG |
+			AMD_PG_SUPPORT_ATHUB;
 		adev->external_rev_id = adev->rev_id + 20;
 		break;
 	case IP_VERSION(10, 1, 2):
